      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What is a KenKen puzzle?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">KenKen is a number logic puzzle where every row and every column contains each number from 1 to N exactly once, and the numbers inside each thick-outlined cage must combine to the cage's target using its operator. It was invented by Japanese math teacher Tetsuya Miyamoto to train arithmetic and logic together.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is KenKen the same as Calcudoku?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Yes. Calcudoku and Mathdoku are the exact same puzzle family with identical rules. "KenKen" is a registered trademark of Nextoy LLC, so unlicensed publishers use the generic names Calcudoku or Mathdoku. GridPaw is not affiliated with, or endorsed by, Nextoy LLC.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is KenKen harder than Sudoku?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Not necessarily. KenKen keeps Sudoku's row-and-column rule and swaps the 3×3 boxes for arithmetic cages, so it exercises mental math as well as logic. Small 4×4 KenKen grids are very beginner-friendly; hard 9×9 grids can be just as demanding as expert Sudoku.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is this KenKen puzzle free?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Yes — GridPaw KenKen is completely free to play in your browser. No download, no account, no payment. Pick Easy 4×4, Medium 6×6 or Hard 9×9 and start solving immediately.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can I play KenKen on mobile?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Yes. The grid is fully responsive and works on any device with a browser. On phones and tablets use the on-screen number pad to enter digits; on a computer you can also type numbers and use the arrow keys to move around the board.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Are all KenKen puzzles solvable without guessing?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Yes — every GridPaw KenKen puzzle has exactly one solution that can be reached through logic alone. The cage arithmetic plus the row and column rules are enough. If you are stuck, the Hint button reveals the correct digit for the selected cell (3 hints per puzzle).</div>
      </details>
